752:Seam carving describes an algorithm usually used to resize pictures \citeapp{Avidan2007}. ``Seams'', in this case, are horizontal or vertical paths of pixels along the picture that are deemed the least important. When resizing the image to be smaller, the least important seams get removed in each step.
